Package: dns-panel-watcher
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Sergey Denisov <4402989@gmail.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/ds1919/dns-panel
Depends: iproute2
Description: DNS Panel watcher: points a pair's service address at the ACTIVE node
 For a DNS Panel pair without a router that does it (Cisco IP SLA and the like): watches the nodes' readiness
 probe and runs the configured commands (a route, NAT) towards the node where it is open.
 Configure /opt/dns-panel/etc/dns-watcher.toml from dns-watcher.example.toml, then start dns-watcher.
